From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Wed, 16 Oct 2024 21:20:42 +0200
Subject: avcodec/rangecoder: eliminate main branch from renorm_encoder()

Backport of upstream commit b2da4c33e31f85b9c755f2cdb08f5db694e90ca9
(avcodec/rangecoder: eliminate main branch from renorm_encoder()).

The 6.1 branch still carries the original branchy form of
renorm_encoder(), whose first arm (c->outstanding_byte < 0) short
circuits the low <= 0xFF00 / low >= 0x10000 cases. GCC miscompiles that
form when the translation unit is built with -O3 together with
-fstack-protector-all (which debian/rules requests through
--toolchain=hardened): the FFV1 range coder then emits a corrupt
extradata.

Observed on x86_64 as a FATE regression of
fate-vsynth1-ffv1-2pass, ffv1-v3-yuv422p10, ffv1-v3-yuv444p16,
ffv1-v3-rgb48 and the vsynth2/vsynth3 equivalents: the encoded stream
is byte identical except that the FFV1 extradata grows from 190 to 298
bytes and is rejected by the decoder with "quant_table_index out of
range".

The upstream rewrite is a pure refactoring (the generated bitstream is
unchanged) that avoids the problematic branch, and it makes the test
pass again with and without -fstack-protector-all.

--- a/libavcodec/rangecoder.h
+++ b/libavcodec/rangecoder.h
@@ -61,25 +61,19 @@ void ff_build_rac_states(RangeCoder *c, int factor, int max_p);
 
 static inline void renorm_encoder(RangeCoder *c)
 {
-    // FIXME: optimize
-        if (c->outstanding_byte < 0) {
-            c->outstanding_byte = c->low >> 8;
-        } else if (c->low <= 0xFF00) {
-            *c->bytestream++ = c->outstanding_byte;
-            for (; c->outstanding_count; c->outstanding_count--)
-                *c->bytestream++ = 0xFF;
-            c->outstanding_byte = c->low >> 8;
-        } else if (c->low >= 0x10000) {
-            *c->bytestream++ = c->outstanding_byte + 1;
-            for (; c->outstanding_count; c->outstanding_count--)
-                *c->bytestream++ = 0x00;
-            c->outstanding_byte = (c->low >> 8) & 0xFF;
-        } else {
-            c->outstanding_count++;
-        }
-
-        c->low     = (c->low & 0xFF) << 8;
-        c->range <<= 8;
+    if (c->low - 0xFF01 >= 0x10000 - 0xFF01U) {
+        int mask = c->low - 0xFF01 >> 31;
+        *c->bytestream = c->outstanding_byte + 1 + mask;
+        c->bytestream += c->outstanding_byte >= 0;
+        for (; c->outstanding_count; c->outstanding_count--)
+            *c->bytestream++ = mask;
+        c->outstanding_byte = c->low >> 8;
+    } else {
+        c->outstanding_count++;
+    }
+
+    c->low     = (c->low & 0xFF) << 8;
+    c->range <<= 8;
 }
 
 static inline int get_rac_count(RangeCoder *c)
